course: dictionary
lesson: 4552
title: Heave and its many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 1
explain: «Heave» is a strong, hard-working word. It can mean to lift, pull or push something heavy with great effort, as in «they heaved the box into the van». The clues are the heavy thing and the big effort.
explain: The same word can also mean a steady rise and fall, as in «the sea heaved». Nothing is being pushed here. Read the words around it: the sea is not lifting anything, it is rising and falling again and again.
explain: Heave can describe a feeling too. «Then he heaved a deep sigh» means he sighed deeply. Ask: what word would fit here? If you swap in breathed out, the sentence still makes sense, so heave shows a big, deep breath.
explain: Context also tells you which kind of word you have. In «one more heave!» heave is a noun, a big pull or push. In «heave the anchor» it is a verb, an action you do. Check the words around it to decide.
fact: Heave is a verb, so its forms are heave, heaves, heaved and heaving.
fact: «Heave» means to lift, pull or push something heavy with great effort.
fact: «Heave a sigh» means to sigh deeply, often to show relief or tiredness.
fact: «Heave» can also mean to rise and fall in a strong, steady way, like the sea.
fact: At sea, «heave to» means to stop a ship, and «hove into view» means came into sight.
exercise: «All four put their shoulders to it and heaved it back.» What does heaved mean here? | Ran very fast | *Pushed or pulled something heavy with great effort | Sang a happy song
exercise: Everyone pulls the rope together and shouts «heave-ho!». What does heave-ho mean? | *Pull together, all at once | Goodbye, see you later | Stop and sit down
exercise: «The sea heaved all night.» What does heaved mean here? | *Rose and fell in a strong, steady way | Shouted loudly | Froze solid
test: «Then he heaves a long, long sigh.» What does heaves mean here? | *Breathes out deeply | Throws something far away | Stops a ship
test: The story says «hove (threw)» the wine-casks overboard. What does hove mean in this sentence? | Sighed | Rose and fell | *Threw
exam: What does «heave» mean in «one more heave!»? | A deep sigh | A wet day | A happy song | *A big pull or push
